From: Mauro DiBenedetto <maurodibenedetto@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] TEST ONLY: special-gated widener for the Lisp spin-word held window

Test instrumentation for the Lisp-side suspend-vs-spin-word deadlock
reproducer.  With CCL::*SPIN-RELEASE-WIDEN-LOOPS* set to a positive
fixnum, every %RELEASE-SPIN-LOCK busy-waits that many iterations
before it clears the word, widening the held window so the race is
reproducible in seconds.  A special variable rather than an
environment lookup, because level-0 code cannot call GETENV and a
special read is safe at any interrupt level; the reproducer arms it
at run time.  Inert at the default 0.

NEVER DELIVER THIS PATCH.  It exists so the Lisp-side reproducer can
be watched red without the level-0 deferral change and green with it,
and it is withheld from every build that is not a reproducer run.
---

--- a/level-0/l0-misc.lisp
+++ b/level-0/l0-misc.lisp
@@ -572,2 +572,15 @@
 ;;; functions.
+;;; TEST ONLY: with CCL::*SPIN-RELEASE-WIDEN-LOOPS* set to a positive
+;;; fixnum, every spin-word release busy-waits that many iterations
+;;; first, widening the held window so the suspend-vs-spin-word race
+;;; is reproducible in seconds.  Inert while the value is 0.  A
+;;; special variable, not an environment lookup: level-0 code cannot
+;;; call GETENV, and a special read is safe at any interrupt level.
+;;; Never deliver this patch.
+(defparameter *spin-release-widen-loops* 0)
+(defun %spin-release-widen-delay ()
+  (let* ((n *spin-release-widen-loops*))
+    (declare (fixnum n))
+    (dotimes (i n))))
+
 #-(or arm-target arm64-target)
@@ -578,2 +591,3 @@
   (defun %release-spin-lock (p)
+    (%spin-release-widen-delay)
     (setf (%get-natural p 0) 0)))
